<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is robotic case packing?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Robotic case packing uses industrial robots to pick products from a conveyor and place them into cases. Delta robots handle lightweight products at high speed; articulated arms handle heavier products with greater flexibility. Vision systems guide picking from moving belts.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">Delta vs. articulated arm for case packing?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Delta: fastest cycles, low payload (ABB IRB 360 variants are rated 1 to 8 kg), suits light food and consumer packages. Articulated arm: slower cycles, wide payload range by model, suits heavy products and mixed-case applications. See also: <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/case/">case packing overview</a>.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">How fast can robotic case packers run?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>It depends on robot type, gripper, products per pick, and case pattern. Delta robots cycle fastest, articulated arms slower. Multi-pick grippers and multi-robot cells raise throughput. Ask suppliers for a rated rate on your products and pattern.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What conveyors does robotic case packing need?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Three conveyors: product infeed (belt with encoder for vision tracking), case conveyor (<a href="/conveyor-functions/indexing-conveyors/">indexing</a> or continuous for case positioning), and case discharge (roller or belt to sealing/palletizing). All coordinate through the cell PLC.</p>

</div>
